course: dictionary
lesson: 6351
title: Movie
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A movie is a story told with moving pictures that you watch on a screen. In the UK, people often call it a film, so movie and film mean the same thing there.
explain: «A family rota, where each person chooses the film in turn, makes movie night fair.» Movie night is a night when the family watches a film together. A rota is a list that takes turns, so each person chooses in turn.
explain: «The movies» can also mean the cinema, the place where you watch films. You can go to the movies with friends, and you can count movies, like «favourite films watched ten times».
explain: «Real robots are not movie robots taking over the world.» Movie robots are made-up robots in stories on a screen. Real robots weld car parts and vacuum floors, so the clues show that movie here means the stories themselves.
fact: A movie is a story told with moving pictures, watched on a screen.
fact: In the UK, a movie is often called a film.
fact: «The movies» means the cinema, the place where you watch films.
fact: You can count movies, and you can say how long a movie is in minutes.
fact: Useful phrases: go to the movies, watch a movie, movie night, movie theater.
exercise: «A family rota, where each person chooses the film in turn, makes movie night fair.» What is a movie night? | A night when the family goes to bed early | *A night when a family watches a film together | A night for cleaning the house | A night when the cinema is closed
exercise: In the UK, people often call a movie a: | A tractor | *A film | A postcard
exercise: Ella says, «Let's go to the movies tonight.» Where are they going? | To a football match | To a shop for bread | To the swimming pool | *To the cinema to watch a film
test: «Real robots are not movie robots taking over the world.» Here, movie robots means: | *Made-up robots in stories on a screen | Robots that help in hospitals | Robots that vacuum floors | Real robots in factories
test: How can you count movies? | By the number of letters in the word | By how loud they are | By the colour of the screen | *By how many you watched, like ten movies
exam: Which phrase means the cinema, the place where you watch films? | Movie robot | Movie night | *The movies | Movie rota
